<title>FRANCE: GEC Alsthom wins substation order.</title>
<headline>GEC Alsthom wins substation order.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>GEC Alsthom said on Tuesday it won a 35 million stg order to supply and install a gas insulated substation at India's Nathpa Jhakri hydroelectric power station.</p>
<p>Under the contract, GEC Alsthom's Power Transmission &amp; Distribution Division will supply two substations from is Aix-les-Bains unit in France. The company will also train the substation's personnel.</p>
<p>The project will be managed by Nathpa Jhakri Power Corp Ltd, a joint venture between the Indian government and the state of Himachal Pradesh.</p>
</text>
